From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:58:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 148/162] hjviewer: hjv-e2e builds hand the waiting room's
 support PC to the next command

Every headless command is a process of its own, and the app keeps the support PCs
its waiting room named in memory only. --hjv-e2e-support-wait now keeps the PC
that arrived in LocalConfig hjv-e2e-support-pc (its ID, key, the ticket's end and
the login), and support_pc reads it when its memory has none, so that the next
command's controller sends the support proof (E2E W6-E4, E4b, E5). Only hjv-e2e
builds have it; the app is one process and needs none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
